"William L. Houts" <abraxas@drizzle.com> wrote:

> I have low vision and would love to play Nethack.
> I'm using the JAWWS 5.1 screen reader. I heard
> somewhere that Nethack was playable with Jaws, but
> I've tried it and it's a confusing junble.

> Can someone tell me how to configure Jaws to work
> with Nethack or vice versa?  Or else direct me to
> a file with that information?

In the runtime configuration file that NetHack uses
at startup, in the MS-Windows version called
"defaults.nh", down toward the bottom of the file is
a commented out section containing a suggested
alternative character set to be used by blind
players, apparently because they are easier to
distinguish on a braille pad than the usual set.

That section include some text describing itself and
how to use it.

Not knowing whether JAWWS is a screen to sound or
screen to touch surface converter makes it hard to
comment past that.

